                  </div>
                  <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">
                    <strong>Bed bugs</strong> crawl slowly, have flat reddish oval bodies (apple-seed size), and shelter within mattress piping, headboards, and electrical plates.
                  </p>
                  <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Fleas</strong> are tiny (1.5–3mm) wingless jumping insects that congregate on domestic pets and carpet piles, delivering bites primarily around lower ankles and shins.
